G4430.b:
⟪πτῶμα⟫, -τος, τό
(< πίπτω), [in LXX: ⟦Judges 14:8|Jg 14:8⟧ (⁨מַפֶּלֶת⁩), ⟦Job 16:15|Jb 16:15⟧ (⟦Job 16:14|14⟧) (⁨פֶּרֶץ⁩), ⟦Isaiah 51:19|Is 51:19⟧ (⁨שֹׁד⁩), Jth 8:19, Wi 4:18, al.;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪a fall⟫, metaph., ⟪a misfortune⟫, ⟪calamity⟫ (Trag., Plat., Polyb., al.; LXX).
⟪2.⟫ That which has fallen;
	⟪(a)⟫ of buildings, ⟪a ruin⟫ (Polyb.);
	⟪(b)⟫ of living creatures, in cl. (poët. only) usually c. gen., νεκρῶν, etc., but also absol., as in late writers and NT, ⟪a fallen body⟫, ⟪a carcase⟫, ⟪corpse⟫: ⟦Matthew 14:12|Mt 14:12⟧ ⟦Matthew 24:28|24:28⟧, ⟦Mark 15:45|Mk 15:45⟧; π. αὐτοῦ, ⟦Mark 6:29|Mk 6:29⟧; αὐτῶν, ⟦Revelation 11:8|Re 11:8⟧, ⟦Revelation 11:9|9⟧ (cf. Rutherford, NPhr., 472 f.).†

G4459.b:
⟪πῶς⟫, interrog. adv., correl. of ὅπως,
⟪1.⟫ prop., in direct questions, ⟪how?⟫: c. indic., ⟦Matthew 12:29|Mt 12:29⟧, ⟦Mark 3:23|Mk 3:23⟧, ⟦Luke 11:18|Lk 11:18⟧, ⟦John 3:4|Jo 3:4⟧, al.; καὶ π., ⟦Mark 4:13|Mk 4:13⟧, ⟦Luke 20:44|Lk 20:44⟧; π. οὖν, ⟦Matthew 12:26|Mt 12:26⟧; π. οὐ, ⟦Matthew 16:11|Mt 16:11⟧, ⟦Luke 12:56|Lk 12:56⟧; in deliberative questions (cf. Bl., § 64, 6), c. subjc., ⟦Matthew 23:33|Mt 23:33⟧ ⟦Matthew 26:54|26:54⟧; π. οὖν, ⟦Romans 10:14|Ro 10:14⟧; π. δέ, ⟦Romans 10:14|Ro 10:14⟧, ⟦Romans 10:15|15⟧; seq. ἄν, c. optat., ⟦Acts 8:31|Ac 8:31⟧.
⟪2.⟫ As sometimes in cl. but more freq. and increasingly so in late writers (v. WM, § 57, 2; Bl., § 70, 2; Thumb, MGr., 192; Jannaris, Gr., App., vi, 13 f.), = ὅπως, ὥς;
	⟪(a)⟫ in indirect discourse: c. indic., ⟦Matthew 6:28|Mt 6:28⟧, ⟦Mark 12:41|Mk 12:41⟧, ⟦Luke 8:36|Lk 8:36⟧, ⟦John 9:15|Jo 9:15⟧, ⟦Acts 9:27|Ac 9:27⟧, al.; c. subjc., ⟦Mark 11:18|Mk 11:18⟧, ⟦Luke 12:11|Lk 12:11⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ in exclamations: ⟦Matthew 21:20|Mt 21:20⟧, ⟦Mark 10:23|Mk 10:23⟧, ⟦Mark 10:24|24⟧, ⟦Luke 12:50|Lk 12:50⟧ ⟦Luke 18:24|18:24⟧, ⟦John 11:36|Jo 11:36⟧.

G4413.b:
B. Superl., ⟪πρῶτος⟫, -η, -ον,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨רִאשׁוֹן⁩, also for ⁨אֶחַד⁩, etc.;] ⟪first⟫,
⟪1.⟫ of Time or Place;
	⟪(a)⟫ absol., as subst., ὁ π.., ⟦Luke 14:18|Lk 14:18⟧, ⟦John 19:32|Jo 19:32⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 14:30|I Co 14:30⟧; ὁ π. καὶ ὁ ἔσχατος, ⟦Revelation 1:17|Re 1:17⟧ ⟦Revelation 2:8|2:8⟧ ⟦Revelation 22:13|22:13⟧; neut., τὸ π., opp. to τ. δεύτερον, ⟦Hebrews 10:9|He 10:9⟧; τὰ π., opp. to τ. ἔσχατα, ⟦Matthew 12:45|Mt 12:45⟧, ⟦Luke 11:26|Lk 11:26⟧, ⟦2 Peter 2:20|II Pe 2:20⟧; anarth., ⟦Matthew 10:2|Mt 10:2⟧; pl., ⟦Matthew 19:30|Mt 19:30⟧, ⟦Mark 10:31|Mk 10:31⟧, ⟦Luke 13:30|Lk 13:30⟧; ἐν πρώτοις (EV, first of all), ⟦1 Corinthians 15:3|I Co 15:3⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ as adj.: πρώτῃ (sc. ἡμέρᾳ) σαββάτου, ⟦Mark 16:9|Mk 16:[9]⟧; φυλακή, opp. to δευτέρα, ⟦Acts 12:10|Ac 12:10⟧; equiv. to adv. in English, ⟦John 8:7|Jo 8:[7]⟧ ⟦John 20:4|20:4⟧, ⟦John 20:8|8⟧, ⟦Acts 27:43|Ac 27:43⟧, ⟦Romans 10:19|Ro 10:19⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 1:16|I Ti 1:16⟧, ⟦1 John 4:19|I Jo 4:19⟧; = πρότερος (v. infr.; cf. M, Pr., 79; Bl., § 11, 5; Thackeray, Gr., 183 f.): c. gen., π. μου ἦν (my chief: Abbott, Jg., 509 ff.; but cf. M, Pr., 245), ⟦John 1:15|Jo 1:15⟧, ⟦John 1:30|30⟧; c. art., ⟦Mark 14:12|Mk 14:12⟧, ⟦Acts 1:1|Ac 1:1⟧, al.; seq. ὁ δεύτερος, etc., ⟦Matthew 22:25|Mt 22:25⟧, ⟦Mark 12:20|Mk 12:20⟧, al.
⟪2.⟫ Of Rank or Dignity, ⟪chief⟫, ⟪principal⟫: ⟦Matthew 20:27|Mt 20:27⟧ ⟦Matthew 22:38|22:38⟧, ⟦Mark 9:35|Mk 9:35⟧, ⟦Ephesians 6:2|Eph 6:2⟧, al.; c. gen., ⟦Mark 12:28|Mk 12:28⟧, ⟦Mark 12:29|29⟧ al.; πόλις (Field, Notes, 124), ⟦Acts 16:12|Ac 16:12⟧; c. art., ⟦Luke 15:22|Lk 15:22⟧ ⟦Luke 19:47|19:47⟧, ⟦Acts 13:50|Ac 13:50⟧, al.
⟪3.⟫ Neut., πρῶτον, as adv., ⟪first⟫, ⟪at the first⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ of Time: ⟦Matthew 8:21|Mt 8:21⟧, ⟦Mark 4:28|Mk 4:28⟧, al.; τὸ π., ⟦John 10:40|Jo 10:40⟧, al.;
	⟪(b)⟫ of Order: ⟦Romans 3:2|Ro 3:2⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 11:18|I Co 11:18⟧, al.

G4464.b:
⟪ῥάβδος⟫, -ου, ἡ
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨מַטֶּה⁩ (e.g. ⟦Genesis 47:31|Ge 47:31⟧, MT, ⁨מַטֶּה⁩, bed), also for ⁨מַקֵּל⁩, ⁨שֵׁבֶט⁩, etc. ;] ⟪a staff, rod⟫: ⟦Hebrews 9:4|He 9:4⟧, ⟦Revelation 11:1|Re 11:1⟧; in particular,
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪a staff⟫, such as is used on a journey: ⟦Matthew 10:10|Mt 10:10⟧, ⟦Mark 6:8|Mk 6:8⟧, ⟦Luke 9:3|Lk 9:3⟧, ⟦Hebrews 11:21|He 11:21⟧ (LXX);
⟪(b)⟫ a ruler's staff, ⟪a sceptre⟫: ⟦Hebrews 1:8|He 1:8⟧ (LXX) ⟦Revelation 2:27|Re 2:27⟧ ⟦Revelation 12:5|12:5⟧ ⟦Revelation 19:15|19:15⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ ⟪a rod⟫ for chastisement (cf. ῥαβδίζω): ἐν ῥ. (v.s. ἐν): ⟦1 Corinthians 4:21|I Co 4:21⟧.†

G4465.b:
* ⟪ῥαβδοῦχος⟫, -ου, ό
(< ῥάβδος, ἔχω), one who carries a rod or staff of office;
⟪(a)⟫ an ⟪umpire or judge⟫ (Plat.);
⟪(b)⟫ in late writers, a Roman ⟪lictor⟫: ⟦Acts 16:35|Ac 16:35⟧, ⟦Acts 16:38|38⟧.†

G4491.b:
⟪ῥίζα⟫, -ης, ἡ
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨שָׁרַשׁ⁩ ;] ⟪a root⟫: ⟦Matthew 3:10|Mt 3:10⟧, ⟦Luke 3:9|Lk 3:9⟧; ἐκ ῥιζῶν, ⟦Mark 11:20|Mk 11:20⟧; ῥ. ἔχειν, ⟦Matthew 13:6|Mt 13:6⟧, ⟦Mark 4:6|Mk 4:6⟧; id. seq. ἐν ἑαυτῷ, fig., ⟦Matthew 13:21|Mt 13:21⟧, ⟦Mark 4:17|Mk 4:17⟧, ⟦Luke 8:13|Lk 8:13⟧. Metaph. (as in various senses in cl.), of cause, origin, source, etc.;
⟪(a)⟫ of things, ῥ. πάντων τ. κακῶν (Eur.), ⟦1 Timothy 6:10|I Ti 6:10⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of persons: of ancestors, ⟦Romans 11:16|Ro 11:16-18⟧; ῥ. πικρίας, ⟦Hebrews 12:15|He 12:15⟧. Of that which springs from a root, ⟪a shoot⟫; metaph., of offspring, ⟦Romans 15:12|Ro 15:12⟧ (LXX), ⟦Revelation 5:5|Re 5:5⟧ ⟦Revelation 22:16|22:16⟧.†
